# Foxinal

SSH connection manager (in progress). Local-first dashboard (nested groups + SSH hosts) + **multi-tab** Local Terminal / SSH sessions via PTY.

## Auth / security

- **No server sync yet** — always local mode
- **First run / no master password** → open dashboard unlocked (no login screen)
- **Optional master password** — Settings → Account → Security; PBKDF2 verifier + **AES-GCM encrypted inventory** (`foxinal-inventory-vault`); plaintext `foxinal-inventory` when unset
- Unlock derives in-memory `CryptoKey`; saves re-encrypt; Lock clears key from memory
- **Lock prefs** (`foxinal-security-prefs`, Settings → Security): auto-lock after idle; lock when app is hidden — suspended while dialogs are open; no window.blur (false-triggers in Tauri)
- Session type: `AppSession` = `{ kind: "local" }` when unlocked

## Stack

| Layer | Tech |
|-------|------|
| Frontend | React 19, TypeScript, Vite 7, xterm, `@tabler/icons-react` |
| Backend | Rust (edition 2021), Tauri 2, `tauri-plugin-pty` |
| Package manager | **pnpm** (see lockfile) |
| Bundle id | `com.foxinal` |

## Layout

- `src/App.tsx` — unlock gate (only when master password exists) + dashboard
- `src/Dashboard.tsx` — navbar + inventory + **session tab strip** (PTYs stay mounted when switching tabs / visiting Dashboard)
- `src/sessions.ts` — tab model (`createLocalTab` / `createHostTab`)
- `src/settings/` — `SettingsDialog` (terminal, account, **security**, about) + `terminalPrefs.ts`
- `src/security/masterPassword.ts` — PBKDF2 verifier + AES key derive
- `src/security/vault.ts` — AES-GCM inventory encrypt/decrypt
- `src/security/session.ts` — enable/change/disable MP + unlock
- `src/security/prefs.ts` + `useLockGuards.ts` — auto-lock / lock-on-blur
- `src/TerminalView.tsx` — local shell or SSH; SSH shows connecting / error+retry overlay; host container must not use padding (FitAddon ignores it and clips the last row — pad `.xterm` instead); reads terminal prefs
- `src/version.ts` — app name/version imported from `package.json` (unlock + Settings about)
- `src-tauri/src/lib.rs` — `default_shell`, `prepare_ssh_launch`, `cleanup_ssh_temp`

## Inventory / SSH

- Storage: `localStorage` `foxinal-inventory` (host secrets plaintext for now)
- Host fields: label, address, port (22), username, password **or** private key
- **Sibling names unique** under each parent (groups + hosts share the namespace)
- **Duplicate host** (copy icon) opens prefilled create dialog (`name copy`, same credentials)
- Dashboard: **search** current folder **and nested** groups/hosts (shows relative path), **list/grid** + **A–Z / Z–A** (`foxinal-inventory-layout`, `foxinal-inventory-sort`)
- **Import / Export** JSON (`foxinal-inventory` v1): at root = whole inventory; inside a group = that group’s subtree / import into that group
- **Double-click group** → enter folder; **double-click host** → new session **tab**
- **Drag-and-drop**: pointer-based (not HTML5 — unreliable in Tauri WebKit); grip `onPointerDown` → window `pointermove`/`pointerup` + `elementsFromPoint` on `[data-fox-drop]`; drop opens destination; blocked for self/descendant / name clash / already there
- Password auth auto-types when SSH password prompt appears; temp keys cleaned via `cleanup_ssh_temp`
- Local Terminal navbar opens another OS shell tab

## UI theme

Clean liquid-glass system in `App.css` (Space Grotesk, `--fox` `#ea580c`, shared spacing/radius tokens). Unlock uses brand header + card; dashboard uses segmented nav + session badge. Terminal font/size/theme via Settings (`foxinal-terminal-prefs`).

## Brand / icons

- Mark: white fox head + terminal `>` / cursor on fox-orange squircle (`#ea580c` → `#c2410c`)
- Master: `app-icon.png` (also `app-icon.svg`) → regenerate with `pnpm tauri icon app-icon.png`
- macOS dock: master PNG must keep ~11% transparent margin per side (~78% content) so optical size matches other apps; do not full-bleed the squircle
- Bundle icons: `src-tauri/icons/` (icns/ico/png)
- Favicon: `public/foxinal.svg`; UI mark stays full-bleed: `public/foxinal-icon.png` via `src/BrandMark.tsx`

## Commands

```bash
pnpm tauri dev      # required for PTY/SSH; Vite :1420
pnpm tauri build
pnpm dev            # frontend only — terminal/SSH fail without Tauri
```

## Release / CI

- Workflow: `.github/workflows/release.yml` — macOS (arm64 + x64) + Linux x64 via `tauri-apps/tauri-action`
- Trigger: push tag `v*` (e.g. `v0.2.0`) or Actions → **release** → Run workflow
- Version is tag-driven: CI runs `scripts/set-version.mjs` so you do **not** need to edit version files by hand before a release
- Manual/local sync if needed: `pnpm version:set 0.2.0` or `pnpm version:patch` (also updates `package.json`, `tauri.conf.json`, `Cargo.toml`)
- `workflow_dispatch` with empty version → auto bump patch from current files
- Creates a **draft** GitHub Release; publish manually in the UI
- Prefer org/repo Workflow permissions → **Read and write**; if greyed out (org policy), add secret `RELEASE_TOKEN` (PAT with contents write) — workflow already uses it when set
- No Apple signing/notarization in CI yet (users may need right-click → Open)

## Conventions

- Prefer Tauri 2 docs; update `capabilities/default.json` when adding plugins
- Never commit `src-tauri/target/`, `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `.env` / `.env.*` (keep `.env.example`), `.pnpm-store/`
- Next: recovery key, OS keychain, host-key UX, jump hosts, server sync
